la Moran","url":"https://www.jerichocentre.org.uk/centre/my_jericho_item/layla-moran"}},{"phase":"career","start":null,"end":null,"title":"Primary school governor","organisation":null,"detail":"She was a primary school governor for two years before her election in 2017.","source":{"title":"Hansard: Education and Local Services, 27 June 2017 (maiden speech)","url":"https://hansard.parliament.uk/Commons/2017-06-27/debates/ACC3BDDE-6E2A-444B-9C6A-EA71C0530F77/EducationAndLocalServices"}},{"phase":"politics","start":null,"end":null,"title":"Leadership programme","organisation":"Liberal Democrats","detail":"She was put on a leadership programme within the Liberal Democrats.","source":{"title":"Jericho Centre: My Jericho: Layla Moran","url":"https://www.jerichocentre.org.uk/centre/my_jericho_item/layla-moran"}},{"phase":"politics","start":"2010","end":"2010","title":"Liberal Democrat candidate for Battersea","organisation":"Liberal Democrats","detail":"She stood in Battersea at the 2010 general election and came third with 7,176 votes.","source":{"title":"Democracy Club: Layla Moran","url":"https://candidates.democracyclub.org.uk/person/2447/layla-moran"}},{"phase":"politics","start":"2012","end":"2012","title":"Liberal Democrat candidate for West Central","organisation":"London Liberal Democrats","detail":"She stood in the West Central constituency at the 2012 London Assembly election and received 10,035 votes.","source":{"title":"Hammersmith and Fulham Council: 2012 London Mayor and Assembly results","url":"https://www.lbhf.gov.uk/councillors-and-democracy/elections/previous-election-results/2012-london-mayor-and-assembly"}},{"phase":"politics","start":"2012-12","end":"2012-12","title":"Selected as prospective candidate for Oxford West and Abingdon","organisation":"Liberal Democrats","detail":"She was selected as the prospective parliamentary candidate for Oxford West and Abingdon in December 2012.","source":{"title":"Jericho Centre: My Jericho: Layla Moran","url":"http